@startuml
title Defense Core — Accepted Run Lifecycle
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "Definition candidate" as Candidate
state "Rejected definition\n(no run exists)" as Rejected #LightGray
state "Run created" as Created
state "RUNNING" as Running
state "SUCCESSFUL terminal" as Successful
state "UNSUCCESSFUL terminal" as Unsuccessful

[*] --> Candidate
Candidate --> Rejected : any definition rule invalid
Rejected --> [*]

Candidate --> Created : complete definition valid
Created --> Running : initial run state and trace committed

Running --> Running : attempt outcome persisted
Running --> Running : retry persisted; same task; no edge
Running --> Running : transition persisted; advance selected task
Running --> Successful : final SUCCESS; no eligible transition
Running --> Unsuccessful : final FAILURE; no eligible transition

Successful --> [*] : terminal trace committed; cleanup complete
Unsuccessful --> [*] : terminal trace committed; cleanup complete

note right of Rejected
This is a validation outcome,
not a persisted workflow-run state.
No execution state is created.
end note

note right of Running
All attempts, retries, selected transitions,
trace positions, and terminal decisions
are scoped to exactly one run.
end note

note bottom of Successful
Choreography terminal path removes
its run-scoped subscription.
end note

note bottom of Unsuccessful
Choreography terminal path removes
its run-scoped subscription.
end note

